mh-mingw/mh-mingw64 name the libraries for MSVC compatibility rather than the
way every other platform does: libicudt.a and libicuin.a instead of
libicudata.a and libicui18n.a (the stubnames exist "so that poorly working FAT
disks and installation programs can work"), no "lib" prefix, and DLLs
installed into bin/ rather than lib/.

None of that describes a static build, which installs no DLLs at all, so this
applies the normal names when ENABLE_SHARED is off.

Beyond the gratuitous difference, the short names are actively broken for a
cross build.  pkgdata composes the static data library's name itself, taking
the "lib" from LIBPREFIX -- which mh-mingw64 leaves empty -- and falling back
to a MinGW branch that hardcodes "lib" for a name containing "icudt".  That
branch is selected by `#if U_PLATFORM == U_PF_MINGW`, i.e. by the platform
pkgdata was *compiled* for, and in a cross build the pkgdata that runs is the
one from --with-cross-build, compiled for the build machine.  So it never
fires, and 33MB of locale data is written as icudt.a, which no install rule
looks for; MINGW_MOVEDLLSTOBINDIR then puts it in bin/ as though it were a
DLL.  What lands in lib/libicudt.a is the 736-byte placeholder from stubdata/,
so anything linking it gets a library with no data in it at all.

--- a/source/config/mh-mingw
+++ b/source/config/mh-mingw
@@ -99,6 +99,21 @@
 I18N_STUBNAME = in
 LIBICU = $(STATIC_PREFIX_WHEN_USED)$(ICUPREFIX)
 
+# A static build produces no DLLs, so none of the naming above applies to anything it installs.
+# Use the same names as every other platform instead, so that consumers need no Windows special
+# case.  LIBPREFIX in particular has to be set rather than spelled out in LIBSICU, because pkgdata
+# composes the data library name from it, and the MinGW branch that would otherwise supply the
+# missing "lib" is chosen by the platform pkgdata was *compiled* for -- which in a cross build is
+# the build machine, so it never triggers and the data library is installed as icudt.a.
+ifneq ($(ENABLE_SHARED),YES)
+LIBPREFIX = lib
+LIBSICU = $(LIBPREFIX)$(STATIC_PREFIX)$(ICUPREFIX)
+LIBICU = $(LIBPREFIX)$(ICUPREFIX)
+DATA_STUBNAME = data
+I18N_STUBNAME = i18n
+MINGW_MOVEDLLSTOBINDIR = NO
+endif
+
 #SH### copied from Makefile.inc
 #SH## for icu-config to test with
 #SH#ICULIBS_COMMON_LIB_NAME="${LIBICU}${COMMON_STUBNAME}${ICULIBSUFFIX}${ICULIBSUFFIX_VERSION}.${SO}"
